  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Around the Gulf of Saint-Tropez — Cogolin, Sainte-Maxime, Grimaud — several confirmed places to stay accept dogs. <strong>Camping Sunêlia L'Argentière</strong>, in Cogolin itself (entrance next to the Château Saint-Maur, 1.5 km from the centre), admits dogs on request at booking, on pitches and most mobile homes, with a supplement. The <strong>Gîte de France ref. G625</strong>, in Sainte-Maxime, has a pool and accepts dogs (the owner has pets of their own). Grimaud's tourist office also publishes a dedicated page listing hotels, campsites, residences and B&Bs that accept dogs in the Grimaud / Port Grimaud area — a useful resource for widening your options.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>On rental platforms, filtering by "pets allowed" is still useful, but a direct message to the owner or campsite often gets you details missing from the listing (number of dogs, excluded breeds, possible deposit).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: according to Cogolin town hall, dogs on a lead are reportedly tolerated on Les Marines de Cogolin beach from 7pm to 1am in season, with a dog shower point nearby — this rule is consistent across several sources, but it remains a seasonal order to reconfirm with the town hall each year before relying on it.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cogolin's harbour and the gulf's beaches round out a stay in the area nicely, as do <a href="/en/fiche-port-grimaud">Port Grimaud</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-sainte-maxime">Sainte-Maxime</a>, a few minutes away by car. On the spot, the <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-toutou-douche-cogolin">Cogolin dog wash</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-veterinaire-riviera-vet">Riviera Vet</a> practice in Sainte-Maxime are handy to keep in mind during your stay.</p>
    </div>

